WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.240
A stitch pattern in the CB1 box is only

2
00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:06.570
a design made up of black
and white squares.

3
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:12.480
To create color work, slip, tuck,
or knit any automatic stitch pattern

4
00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:16.380
technique, you first need
to instruct the machine.

5
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:21.600
This tutorial will cover how to tell
the CB1 box which knitting carriage you're

6
00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:29.920
using and how to instruct it to position
the stitch pattern on the needle bed.

7
00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:31.780
From the main menu,

8
00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:40.000
we'll choose the positioning program icon,
then choose the pattern positioning icon.

9
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:45.040
We'll choose which carriage we're going
to be using, either the K carriage,

10
00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.480
the Lace carriage, or the G
carriage with the icons.

11
00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:52.400
Then we can choose the pattern range,

12
00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:56.720
either a single motif
or repeat the pattern.

13
00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:03.560
Next, we'll enter in the stitch world
pattern number or the 900 number series,

14
00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:09.080
901 through 999, if you created
your own stitch pattern.

15
00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:15.340
Now, by default, the stitch pattern is
automatically centered on the needle bed.

16
00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:19.260
If you want to shift the stitch pattern
one way or the other,

17
00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:24.880
enter in the number of needles,
left or right, that you want to shift.

18
00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:29.570
Your stitch pattern is now positioned
and you're ready to start knitting.

19
00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:35.210
Now, if this indicator displays a stitch
variation is currently active,

20
00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:41.930
use the Variations menu to select or
deselect stitch variations as needed.

21
00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:44.320
We'll talk more about
this in another video.

